{competency_questions}

ELEMENT CATALOG:
{element_catalog}

SYNTHETIC FEW-SHOT EXAMPLES — syntax guidance only:
{few_shot_08}

Define all classes, object properties and data properties clearly; retain justified axioms, subclass/type statements, domain/range semantics, human-readable labels and useful descriptions. Use consistent prefixes and stable absolute IRIs matching element_catalog; never rename or change the kind of catalog entries. Preserve the entire conceptual model, not a snippet.

Retain CQ provenance as annotations: declare <https://example.org/yonsei/relatedCQ> a owl:AnnotationProperty. For EVERY catalog element, emit one <https://example.org/yonsei/relatedCQ> literal annotation for every cq_ids entry (e.g. "CQ1"). These are provenance annotations, not domain properties or domain assertions. Include every catalog element and all its accepted CQ links in the full ontology.
